## Langfuse exposes decision-model evaluators through its public API

Source: Langfuse — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-11-25-decision-model-evaluators-api
Published: 2026-11-25
Channel: news

Langfuse is an AI observability and evaluation platform used to record and assess application behavior. Its decision-model evaluators can now be managed through the stable public evaluators API, alongside its model-judge and code evaluators. The change gives teams an API path for managing these evaluator definitions rather than relying solely on manual configuration.

To use it, create an evaluator with the decision-model type. Its definition includes questions and their allowed answers, a provider and decision model, and a mapping from observation data to named state keys used by the questions. Questions can use choices, ordered scores or boolean answers. Teams can then keep the definitions in version control and attach them to evaluation rules from a deployment pipeline, according to Langfuse. The announcement describes the management interface; it does not report an independent measurement of evaluator quality.

Why it matters: Teams maintaining evaluations in deployment pipelines can review whether evaluator definitions belong alongside their application configuration.

